## 16. APPLICATION STATES AND ERROR HANDLING

Implement all meaningful states.

### Initial state

The 3D environment is already rendered and slowly animating.

The music library is visible.

No track is falsely marked as playing.

The interface indicates that the user can select a song or connect an audio source.

### Track selected

Display the correct title and artist.

Resolve the track's audio source.

Show a loading state if necessary.

### Playing

Update the progress bar using the actual playback position.

Run the audio analysis.

Animate the scene using the actual signal.

### Paused

Pause the audio and stop advancing the playback position.

Return the visualiser to a gentle idle animation rather than freezing the entire scene.

### Track unavailable

Explain that the recording is not available for in-app playback.

Offer a supported alternative where appropriate.

### Audio failure

Display a concise error message and allow the user to retry or select another source.

### WebGL failure

Keep the library and playback interface accessible wherever possible, and explain that 3D rendering could not be initialised.

Never display a fake success state.

