## 18. STRICTLY PROHIBITED IMPLEMENTATION SHORTCUTS

Do not:
- Replace the 3D scene with a static image.
- Create a flat 2D imitation of a 3D environment.
- Use a prerecorded animation and claim it responds to live audio.
- Make the wireframe sphere rotate without any real audio-reactive deformation.
- Populate the library with fabricated recordings.
- Claim that a song is playing when no audio is being played.
- Create buttons that do nothing.
- Display fake track durations, playback positions, or audio measurements.
- Leave sliders disconnected from the rendering system.
- Implement visualiser modes that all look identical.
- Use an excessively bright interface that destroys the dark cyberpunk atmosphere.
- Apply so much dithering that the interface becomes unreadable.
- Allow the side panels to consume most of the screen.
- Add AI music generation features.
- Leave the application as a nonfunctional visual prototype.
- Introduce unnecessary login requirements when the basic experience can work without them.

Use mock data only for legitimate interface previews and clearly distinguish mock metadata from real playback.

